 ASSR with its administrative center in Balaklava. After World War II in 1957, it became part of Sevastopol city municipality. All populated places of the district became incorporated with the city of Sevastopol. In 1976, the city of Inkerman was reinstated as a city. Population: 27,620 (2014 Census).\nThe district is subdivided into three municipality (councils): Inkerman city council, Orlyne Village Council, and Ternivka Village Council. Balaklavskyi District borders with Bakhchysarai Raion and Yalta Municipality."]},"3832":{"n":"Казачья Бухта","p":[["c/c8/Sevastopol_Museum_and_memorial_complex_35th_Coast_Battery_IMG_1345_1725.jpg","Sevastopol Museum and memorial complex 35th Coast Battery 1…","Alexxx1979","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.67],["0/07/Sevastopol_Black_Sea_IMG_4601_1725.jpg","Sevastopol Black Sea 1725","Alexxx1979","CC BY-SA 3.0",0.67],["1/1e/Sevastopol_125_%288642731271%29.jpg","Sevastopol 125","Alexxx Malev from Taganrog, Russia","CC BY-SA 2.0",0.67],["b/ba/Natural_arch_-_panoramio_%281811%29.jpg","Natural arch","Y3","CC BY-SA 3.0",1.5],["1/1d/Sevastopol%2C_the_Blue_bay_-_%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%B0%2C_%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%B0%D1%8F_%D0%B1%D1%83%D1%85%D1%82%D0%B0_-_panoramio.jpg","Sevastopol, the Blue bay - Казачка, Голубая бухта","Pavlo68","CC BY 3.0",0.67],["a/a4/Untitled1_-_panoramio_%28114%29.jpg","Untitled1","Y3","CC BY-SA 3.0",1.5]]}}}